    <string name="help_canvas_title">Canvas</string>
    <string name="help_appearance_body">Pick the app\u2019s colour scheme: five light and three dark palettes. The choice is fixed \u2014 the app does not follow the system\u2019s dark mode or wallpaper colours.</string>
    <string name="help_drawing_body">Handedness: which side of the canvas the tool rail sits on.\n\nStylus only: only the pen draws; fingers still move, zoom, and rotate the canvas.\n\nPen button: what the stylus side button does \u2014 switch to the eraser, or pick a colour while held.\n\nEraser end: which eraser the pen\u2019s eraser tip uses.\n\nPressure: how pen pressure maps to the brush. Softer reaches full effect early; Harder needs a firm press.\n\nSnap right angles: two-finger rotation clicks into 0\u00b0, 90\u00b0, 180\u00b0, and 270\u00b0.</string>
    <string name="help_feedback_body">Haptics: brief vibrations when you undo, cross slider marks, pick colours, or reorder layers.</string>
    <string name="help_storage_body">Gallery sync keeps a copy of every painting in Pictures/\u5e2e\u4f60Draw, updated as you paint. A painting with a visible tracing image keeps a second copy that includes it. Deleting a painting can take its gallery copies along.\n\nUndo limit: how many steps and how much storage each painting\u2019s undo history may keep.</string>
    <string name="help_mixer_body">Pigment mixes like real paint: blue and yellow make green, and colours deepen as they combine. RGB mixes like light on a screen \u2014 faster, but muddier for paint-like work. Pigment mixing is powered by Mixbox (CC BY-NC 4.0).</string>
    <string name="help_shortcuts_body">These work with a keyboard attached \u2014 DeX, a Chromebook, or a tablet with a keyboard cover.</string>
    <string name="help_studio_body">Everything is saved automatically as you draw \u2014 there is no save button.\n\nTap + to start a new painting. Hold a painting (or tap \u22ee) to open, rename, duplicate, share, copy to the gallery, or delete it \u2014 deleting can take the gallery copies along.</string>
    <string name="help_new_canvas_body">Pick a size preset, or Custom to type your own. \u201cFits N layers\u201d is this device\u2019s memory budget for that size: bigger canvases allow fewer layers.\n\nPaper sets the background colour. Transparent exports with a see-through background \u2014 PNG keeps it, JPEG fills it white.</string>
    <string name="help_brush_sheet_body">These controls edit the selected brush preset and are kept until you reset it. The strip previews the stroke. Reset restores the factory tuning.\n\nTip: tapping the brush that is already active opens this sheet.</string>
    <string name="help_brush_stroke_body">Size: brush diameter in pixels.\n\nOpacity: how much the paper shows through the finished stroke.\n\nFlow: how much paint each dab lays down; low flow builds up as you go over the same spot.</string>
    <string name="help_brush_tip_body">Hardness: how sharp the stroke\u2019s edge is.\n\nSpacing: the distance between dabs, as a share of the brush diameter \u2014 low is a smooth line, high a string of stamps.\n\nShape: round or flat; a flat tip adds an aspect ratio.\n\nOrientation: what rotates a flat tip \u2014 a fixed angle, the stylus direction, or the stroke direction.</string>
    <string name="help_brush_dynamics_body">Pressure: three curves map pen pressure to size, opacity, and flow; the four knots shape each curve from light to firm.\n\nTilt: how holding the pen flatter changes size and opacity; Elongate stretches the tip along the tilt.\n\nVelocity: how fast strokes change size and opacity, and the speed that counts as fast.\n\nJitter: random per-dab variation in size and position.\n\nStabilizer: smooths hand wobble; high values lag behind your hand.</string>
    <string name="help_brush_paint_body">Grain: paper tooth \u2014 the pencil\u2019s speckled texture.\n\nWatercolor brushes replace this group with Water (how wet the brush is), Spread (how far colour bleeds), Granulation (pigment settling into texture), and Edge darkening (darker rims as the paint dries).\n\nPigment: blend with paint already on the canvas instead of only covering it. Dilution: how much the colour is thinned. Both appear while pigment mixing is on in Settings.\n\nBuffer: Max keeps a stroke from darkening over itself; Accumulate lets it build up.</string>
    <string name="help_fill_body">Tap an area to fill it with the current colour.\n\nTolerance: how different a pixel may be and still belong to the same area.\nExpand: grows the fill a few pixels under the surrounding lines, hiding pale fringes.\nOpacity: how much of what is underneath shows through.\nContiguous: fill only the connected area; off fills every matching area at once.\nAnti-alias: softens the fill\u2019s edge.\nReference: Current layer fills within this layer\u2019s paint; Composite uses the whole picture.</string>
    <string name="help_smudge_body">Drags paint along the stroke, like a finger through wet paint.\n\nStrength: how far paint is pulled.\nPickup: how much colour the finger picks up and carries.\nPigment: blend the carried colour into what is underneath.</string>
    <string name="help_water_body">A colourless wet brush: it rewets paint and lets it run without adding colour \u2014 for soft edges and wet-on-wet blends. The water dries on its own within half a minute; the moved paint stays.\n\nWater: how much the brush carries. Spread: how far the wetness travels.</string>
    <string name="help_blur_body">Softens whatever you stroke over.\n\nStrength: how much each pass softens. Radius: how wide an area blends together. Spacing and the pressure curve work like a brush\u2019s.</string>
    <string name="help_eyedropper_body">Lifts a colour from the canvas into the brush.\n\nComposite samples the whole picture; Current layer only this layer. Radius averages an area \u2014 0 picks the exact pixel.\n\nTip: holding a finger still on the canvas picks a colour at any time.</string>
    <string name="help_layers_body">Paint stacks in layers; the top row is the front. Tap a row to paint on it.\n\nThe eye hides a layer. The percentage opens its opacity slider. The handle drags to reorder. Hold a row (or tap \u22ee) to rename, duplicate, merge down, clear, or delete it \u2014 and to set two locks: Alpha lock paints only where paint already is; Lock protects the layer from any edit. Blend modes change how a layer colours what is below it.\n\nPaper sets the background colour. The header\u2019s \u22ee menu flattens everything into one layer. The layer limit depends on canvas size and device memory.</string>
    <string name="help_color_body">The ring picks the hue; the square sets saturation and brightness. Fine-tune with the sliders, or type hex and RGB values.\n\nHold the current colour to add it to the palette. Tap the previous colour to swap back.\n\nPalettes keep saved colours \u2014 create your own with +. Hold a swatch to replace, pick, move, or delete it.\n\nThe mixing dish blends two colours: set wells A and B, drag the slider for the in-between steps, tap a step to use it.</string>
    <string name="help_reference_body">Pin a photo over your painting to trace or compare; two fingers on the canvas move, scale, and rotate it.\n\nThe reference never enters shares or exports. With gallery sync on, a second gallery copy that includes it is kept alongside. It uses the memory of one layer.</string>
    <string name="help_canvas_body">Draw with one finger or a pen; two fingers move, zoom, and rotate the canvas. Tap two fingers to undo, three to redo \u2014 or hold the undo and redo buttons to see how deep the history goes. Tap the pill that appears after moving the view to reset it.\n\nHold a finger still to pick a colour. Hold the colour chip for the colours you last painted with. Tap the active tool again to open its settings.\n\nThe sliders beside the rail set brush size and opacity. The \u22ee menu shares and exports, renames the painting, pins a tracing image, toggles composition guides, and hides all controls in Focus mode.</string>
</resources>
